Q3:
Function Calling lets an LLM output a structured JSON object that represents a call to an external tool (API, database, calculator, code executor, etc.).

the model produces:(json )
{
  "name": "getWeather",
  "arguments": { "city": "Colombo" }
}

Your application then executes the function, gets real data, and sends the result back to the LLM.
The LLM “plans” → your tool “executes” → the LLM “responds”.
